{"id":"e17t3","name":"Merge Subscription Periods","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>subscriptions</b> has the columns <code>sub_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>start_date</code> and <code>end_date</code> (dates). A subscription covers every day from <code>start_date</code> to <code>end_date</code>, both included. An <code>end_date</code> that is <code>NULL</code> means the subscription is still active: treat it as <code>2026-12-31</code>.</p>\n<p>Subscriptions of a customer can overlap or follow each other. Two periods are merged when they overlap or when one starts the day right after the other ends.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the merged periods with the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>period_start</code>, <code>period_end</code> and <code>days</code> (number of days covered, both ends included), sorted by <code>customer_id</code>, then <code>period_start</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>subscriptions</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>sub_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>start_date</th><th>end_date</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-01-01</td><td>2026-03-31</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2026-02-01</td><td>2026-02-15</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2026-04-01</td><td>2026-04-30</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>2026-06-01</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>2026-01-10</td><td>2026-01-20</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>2026-01-22</td><td>2026-01-25</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>period_start</th><th>period_end</th><th>days</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-01-01</td><td>2026-04-30</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-06-01</td><td>2026-12-31</td><td>214</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-01-10</td><td>2026-01-20</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-01-22</td><td>2026-01-25</td><td>4</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["intervalles qui se chevauchent","îlots","MAX cumulé","dates de fin NULL"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"subscriptions":{"columns":[["sub_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["start_date","DATE"],["end_date","DATE"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-01-01","2026-03-31"],[2,1,"2026-02-01","2026-02-15"],[3,1,"2026-04-01","2026-04-30"],[4,1,"2026-06-01",null],[5,2,"2026-01-10","2026-01-20"],[6,2,"2026-01-22","2026-01-25"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","period_start","period_end","days"],"rows":[[1,"2026-01-01","2026-04-30",120],[1,"2026-06-01","2026-12-31",214],[2,"2026-01-10","2026-01-20",11],[2,"2026-01-22","2026-01-25",4]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"subscriptions":{"columns":[["sub_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["start_date","DATE"],["end_date","DATE"]],"rows":[[1,5,"2026-05-01","2026-05-01"],[2,5,"2026-05-02","2026-05-02"],[3,5,"2026-05-01","2026-05-01"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","period_start","period_end","days"],"rows":[[5,"2026-05-01","2026-05-02",2]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}